=A0<div><br></div><div>There will be 2 days of workshops (Sept 21-22) and 3=
 days of single-track 30-minute talks (Sept 23-25). We will be able to host=
 <b>up to 4 workshops</b> and <b>~30 talks. </b>All talks and workshop sess=
ions will be recorded, transcribed, and added to the corpus that PI's AI in=
frastructure is trained on.<div><ul><li><b>Workshops</b>: The format is 4-6=
 Zoom sessions of ~60-90 minutes each over 2 days, with some sort of asynch=
ronous co-working and discussion on Discord between sessions. The target wo=
rkshop size is 30-50 participants. There should be a clear learning or skil=
l development outcome for participants, at the frontiers of protocol wrangl=
ing or theory (ie in emerging areas, not established ones). An honorarium w=
ill be available for workshop organizers. To ensure a resilient agenda, eve=
ry workshop proposal <b>requires at least two organizers</b>.</li><li><b>Ta=
lks</b>: For papers, the expectation is a researched 25 minute talk with 5 =
minute Q&amp;A, preferably accompanied by either a preprint (academic arXiv=
 style) aimed at a specialist audience or draft magazine feature style aime=
d at a general audience. Prizes totaling $6000 will be awarded to the best =
talks. We may offer publishing opportunities in our magazine,=C2=A0<i>Proto=
colized,=C2=A0</i>for selected talks, abstracts and articles.</li></ul><spa=
n><div>Other things being equal, we will prioritize workshop and talk propo=
